WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.768 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Hi, Paula!
-Hello, hello!

00:00:01.768 --> 00:00:04.004 size:75% position:38%
-You look wonderful!
-Thank you so much.

00:00:04.004 --> 00:00:07.841
I Kondo'd my closet so hard,
I had to go get an outfit.

00:00:07.841 --> 00:00:08.608 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, wow!
[ Laughter ]

00:00:08.608 --> 00:00:11.411 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Because all I had left
was like a bra and sweatpants

00:00:11.411 --> 00:00:13.146 align:start size:94% position:6%
that I only wear
when I have the flu.

00:00:13.146 --> 00:00:14.447 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, gotcha.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:14.447 --> 00:00:16.116 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, I got a little suit.
-That's the danger.

00:00:16.116 --> 00:00:17.851 align:start size:94% position:6%
The danger of Kondo'ing.
You over-Kondo'd.

00:00:17.851 --> 00:00:20.086 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Hold on.
Ahh.

00:00:20.086 --> 00:00:23.857 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:23.857 --> 00:00:25.959 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You're looking at my butt
right now.

00:00:25.959 --> 00:00:26.893 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
Hi.

00:00:26.893 --> 00:00:28.862 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I have known you
for a very long time.

00:00:28.862 --> 00:00:30.530 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So long.
-And I met you as a writer

00:00:30.530 --> 00:00:32.632 align:start size:94% position:6%
at "SNL,"
and everyone who ever worked

00:00:32.632 --> 00:00:33.500 line:92%
in a writer's room with you

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:36.169 align:start size:94% position:6%
knew you to be
the funniest person on Earth.

00:00:36.169 --> 00:00:37.137 line:92%
And now it's really exciting,

00:00:37.137 --> 00:00:39.172 align:start size:94% position:6%
because you're acting
a lot more now,

00:00:39.172 --> 00:00:40.740 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the world is seeing
how funny you are.

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:44.177 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I am. I'm aging into these
older-lady characters.

00:00:44.177 --> 00:00:47.147 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was born at 50.
I was born a matron.

00:00:47.147 --> 00:00:49.416 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I always wore
the gray spray in my hair

00:00:49.416 --> 00:00:51.684 align:start size:94% position:6%
and played the Mother Superior
in 8th grade

00:00:51.684 --> 00:00:54.487 size:84% position:42%
in "Sound of Music,"
and now I'm actually --

00:00:54.487 --> 00:00:58.525 align:start size:94% position:6%
of an approximate age --
I'm nearing an approximate age

00:00:58.525 --> 00:01:01.594 align:start size:94% position:6%
where I can play a lady,
say, in her 50s.

00:01:01.594 --> 00:01:03.129 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-That's wonderful.

00:01:03.129 --> 00:01:04.531 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the world is so happy
to have it.

00:01:04.531 --> 00:01:07.734 size:81% position:41%
And now you've created
so many characters --

00:01:07.734 --> 00:01:08.401 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
too many to list --

00:01:08.401 --> 00:01:10.804 align:start size:94% position:6%
for wonderful actors at "SNL"
over the years.

00:01:10.804 --> 00:01:12.172
You have a new character.
-I have a new character.

00:01:12.172 --> 00:01:13.339 align:start size:94% position:6%
-For yourself, now,
which is really exciting.

00:01:13.339 --> 00:01:16.776
-That I just created just to
soothe myself and my friends.

00:01:16.776 --> 00:01:18.945 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's just kind of
not fully flushed out yet,

00:01:18.945 --> 00:01:20.914 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I was gonna try it out
on you.

00:01:20.914 --> 00:01:22.849 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Great.
-It's -- It got inspired

00:01:22.849 --> 00:01:26.219 align:start size:94% position:6%
when I was drinking some tea,
some green tea,

00:01:26.219 --> 00:01:30.490 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I found what was
on the box so comforting.

00:01:30.490 --> 00:01:32.325 align:start size:94% position:6%
Come over here, Seth.
-Okay. Come sit next you?

00:01:32.325 --> 00:01:35.495
-The world is just such a scary
place now, so I just --

00:01:35.495 --> 00:01:36.463 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay.
-I want you to feel --

00:01:36.463 --> 00:01:37.897 size:75% position:38%
-And what's the name
of your character?

00:01:37.897 --> 00:01:39.833 align:start size:94% position:6%
-My character's name
is Nana Teabags.

00:01:39.833 --> 00:01:41.835 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay, gotcha.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:41.835 --> 00:01:43.570 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, just come over here
with me.

00:01:43.570 --> 00:01:44.003 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Okay.

00:01:44.003 --> 00:01:45.872 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And just really
park your head on my bosom.

00:01:45.872 --> 00:01:47.974 align:start size:94% position:6%
Just go --
-Okay. Like that?

00:01:47.974 --> 00:01:50.510 align:start size:94% position:6%
Okay.
-Just right in the bike rack.

00:01:50.510 --> 00:01:52.245 align:start size:94% position:6%
Okay.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:52.245 --> 00:01:54.714 align:start size:94% position:6%
Now just close your eyes.
-Okay. The bike rack?

00:01:54.714 --> 00:01:56.483 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And I'm just gonna
read about tea.

00:01:56.483 --> 00:01:57.951 align:start size:94% position:6%
You ready?
-Yeah.

00:01:57.951 --> 00:02:00.019 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:00.019 --> 00:02:03.857 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Through the screened
front door,

00:02:03.857 --> 00:02:06.926 align:start size:94% position:6%
zingy lemongrass
and spritely spearmint

00:02:06.926 --> 00:02:14.534 align:start size:94% position:6%
coax contemplative pan-fired
green teas to come play.

00:02:14.534 --> 00:02:15.201 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:15.201 --> 00:02:18.238 align:start size:94% position:6%
Calmly,
lemon verbena opens the door

00:02:18.238 --> 00:02:21.574 align:start size:94% position:6%
and invites them all
to a cup of tea.

00:02:21.574 --> 00:02:22.742 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:22.742 --> 00:02:24.043 align:start size:94% position:6%
Now, wait.
There's a little bit more.

00:02:24.043 --> 00:02:24.878 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, okay.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:24.878 --> 00:02:29.215 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Giggling -- Giggling notes
of curious chai tea

00:02:29.215 --> 00:02:33.753 align:start size:94% position:6%
peek mischievously
from behind a painted screen.

00:02:33.753 --> 00:02:36.923 align:start size:94% position:6%
They summon us
and gently suggest

00:02:36.923 --> 00:02:38.892 line:92%
that we join their spicy hang

00:02:38.892 --> 00:02:41.794 align:start size:94% position:6%
and leave our pantaloons
at the door.

00:02:41.794 --> 00:02:44.364 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:44.364 --> 00:02:51.938 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:51.938 --> 00:02:53.506 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You have such --
-Go back and sit there,

00:02:53.506 --> 00:02:55.275 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause I'm starting
to get straight.

00:02:55.275 --> 00:02:56.109 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:56.109 --> 00:02:58.511 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You have such --
-My 10% went to 12%.

00:02:58.511 --> 00:02:59.078 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Cheers ]

00:02:59.078 --> 00:03:00.413 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You're up to 12?
That's a new record.

00:03:00.413 --> 00:03:02.348 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm up to 12
when I'm sitting with you.

00:03:02.348 --> 00:03:03.383 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're foxy.
-Thank you.

00:03:03.383 --> 00:03:05.485 align:start size:94% position:6%
Your diction is such
that you were just, like,

00:03:05.485 --> 00:03:07.320 align:start size:94% position:6%
blowing those words
across the top of my hair.

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:09.489 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
Just very Sally Kellerman.

00:03:09.489 --> 00:03:12.725 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-Blue-cheese dressings.

00:03:12.725 --> 00:03:13.259 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:13.259 --> 00:03:16.396 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You had another incredible
performance this year,

00:03:16.396 --> 00:03:18.631 align:start size:94% position:6%
and even Jesse Eisenberg,
a previous guest,

00:03:18.631 --> 00:03:19.399 size:78% position:39% line:92%
was shouting you out.

00:03:19.399 --> 00:03:22.101
An episode of "Documentary Now,"
you played --

00:03:22.101 --> 00:03:24.871 align:start size:94% position:6%
You basically channeled
Elaine Stritch.

00:03:24.871 --> 00:03:25.471 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I channeled her.

00:03:25.471 --> 00:03:27.607 align:start size:94% position:6%
I did not do
a real impression of her,

00:03:27.607 --> 00:03:29.142 align:start size:94% position:6%
because no one can be
Elaine Stritch.

00:03:29.142 --> 00:03:30.810 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You grabbed her spirit.
-Yes.

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:33.379 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Because there was this famous
moment in this documentary

00:03:33.379 --> 00:03:34.447 align:start size:94% position:6%
about the "Company"
cast recording

00:03:34.447 --> 00:03:36.916 align:start size:94% position:6%
where she was having issues
singing her song,

00:03:36.916 --> 00:03:38.051 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Ladies Who Lunch."
-Yes.

00:03:38.051 --> 00:03:40.320 size:81% position:41%
-You, in this episode,
were singing a song,

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:42.622 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I Gotta Go,"
also having difficulties.

00:03:42.622 --> 00:03:44.958 align:start size:94% position:6%
Let's take a look at a clip
real fast.

00:03:44.958 --> 00:03:46.726 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"I Gotta Go,"
take 11.

00:03:46.726 --> 00:03:51.097
-Benedict, just so we're clear,
earlier, many times I mentioned

00:03:51.097 --> 00:03:54.267
I had an eye-doctor appointment
to get my eyes scraped,

00:03:54.267 --> 00:03:56.769 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I have already
taken the medication,

00:03:56.769 --> 00:03:58.838 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it's ripping
through my system.

00:03:58.838 --> 00:04:01.241 align:start size:94% position:6%
So we need
to be brisk with this.

00:04:01.241 --> 00:04:02.609 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Let's just do it.

00:04:02.609 --> 00:04:06.112 size:75% position:38% line:92%
♪♪ And I gotta go ♪♪

00:04:06.112 --> 00:04:09.349 align:start size:94% position:6%
♪♪ I should do better
or different than this ♪♪

00:04:09.349 --> 00:04:10.650 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
No [bleep] kidding.

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:12.452 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:12.452 --> 00:04:15.555 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:15.555 --> 00:04:19.259 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was so --
so joyous to watch you.

00:04:19.259 --> 00:04:20.526 line:92%
I hope you enjoyed doing this.

00:04:20.526 --> 00:04:23.463 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was so beyond --
I'm such a theater nerd.

00:04:23.463 --> 00:04:25.632 align:start size:94% position:6%
I got my degree in theater
in college.

00:04:25.632 --> 00:04:28.501 align:start size:94% position:6%
I always did theater,
and it was --

00:04:28.501 --> 00:04:31.104 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I stage-managed "Company"
when I was young.

00:04:31.104 --> 00:04:34.107
And my mom actually played
that Elaine Stritch role.

00:04:34.107 --> 00:04:36.109
She hadn't done theater
since high school, and she said,

00:04:36.109 --> 00:04:39.345
"I turned 40, and I'm gonna
get my license finally --

00:04:39.345 --> 00:04:41.381 align:start size:94% position:6%
driver's license --
and I'm gonna be in a show."

00:04:41.381 --> 00:04:43.716 align:start size:94% position:6%
And she played --
She sang "Ladies Who Lunch."

00:04:43.716 --> 00:04:45.051 align:start size:94% position:6%
So it was, like,
a perfect little

00:04:45.051 --> 00:04:47.787 align:start size:94% position:6%
beautiful thing,
but we kept laughing

00:04:47.787 --> 00:04:49.455 align:start size:94% position:6%
because we loved
doing it so much,

00:04:49.455 --> 00:04:51.391 align:start size:94% position:6%
and learning all the music
that we kept, like --

00:04:51.391 --> 00:04:53.293 align:start size:94% position:6%
We finished, and they're like,
"Great, we're wrapped,"

00:04:53.293 --> 00:04:55.228
and we're like,
"Can't we go to Seattle in a van

00:04:55.228 --> 00:05:00.199
and do this at local theaters?"
[ Laughter ]

